# Forward mode in the arguments of a reciprocal sum (D[force-matching-forward],
# #726), on the CPU: Psi along lambda, along the field q0, and along lambda
# and a constant of a pair term, against dE/dlambda (D161) and the
# derivative of the tangent of D379 (the transpose identity), in double and
# mixed precision. Inputs/direction_pme.py appends the checks to the program
# of Inputs/tangent_pme.py.
#
# REQUIRES: python-api
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/tangent_pme.py 1e-12 %t/base.mlir
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/direction_pme.py %t/base.mlir %t/double.mlir
# RUN: mdir-opt %t/double.mlir %md_passes \
# RUN:     --convert-md-to-md-exec="skin=0.2 width=64" %md_exec_passes \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_loops_to_llvm --convert-ub-to-llvm --reconcile-unrealized-casts \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s
#
# Central differences along the directions, by md-check-derivatives, of
# the energy for `direction` and of the forces for `direction_forces`, at
# the step 0.1 (exact but for the rounding: the energy and the forces are
# quadratic in the charges and linear in eps). It aborts with a message on a
# value outside the tolerance; the mark is printed after the checks.
#
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/tangent_pme.py 1e-12 %t/fd-base.mlir fd
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/direction_pme.py %t/fd-base.mlir %t/fd.mlir fd
# RUN: mdir-opt %t/fd.mlir --md-check-derivatives="step=0.1 atol=1e-9 rtol=1e-8" \
# RUN:     %md_passes --convert-md-to-md-exec="skin=0.2 width=64" %md_exec_passes \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_loops_to_llvm --convert-ub-to-llvm --reconcile-unrealized-casts \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FD
#
# FD: {{^-726$}}
#
# The checks of forward mode follow a mark, -726, after those of the
# program against the Ewald sum, which are not read here (the tolerance
# 1e-12 given to the script is that of forward mode, below the accuracy of
# the mesh). Each prints the relative error and then 1 within 1e-12.
# CHECK: {{^-726$}}
# CHECK-COUNT-5: {{^}}{{[0-9.e+-]+}}{{$}}{{[[:space:]]+}}1{{$}}
